<title>JAPAN: Japan magnesium demand falls 2.7 percent in 1996.</title>
<headline>Japan magnesium demand falls 2.7 percent in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese magnesium demand fell 2.7 percent in 1996 to 29,654 tonnes, the Japan Magnesium Association said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Figures for Japanese magnesium demand were as follows, in tonnes with percent change from the year before:</p>
<p>			 1996   change</p>
<p> Castings	   2,308   +47.1</p>
<p> Aluminium	 21,718    +1.0</p>
<p> Other		4,295   -22.4</p>
<p> Domestic total   28,321   -1.0</p>
<p> Exports		  73  -62.0</p>
<p> Imports	     1,260  -24.8</p>
<p> TOTAL		29,654   -2.7</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
